<http://data.silknow.org/object/f79eeffc-12d0-3a19-8306-584d62ffbd29/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Description: Dress fabric of woven silk and metal thread.\nDark blue ground, weft-faced plain weave, with a dense, small-scale pattern woven with metal thread [silver-gilt open S-wound on a yellow silk core] with small details in red silk. There is a vertical line linking an iris above a small carnation and other unidentifiable flower heads. Immediately below the irises is a horizontal line of slightly diagonal bunches of 3 red and gold buds.  Half way between the irises is another horizontal line, this time it is a series of left-curving stems with 3 flowers, including an iris. These elements combine to create an almost solid design with swirling movement."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/f79eeffc-12d0-3a19-8306-584d62ffbd29> .

<https://sws.geonames.org/130758/>
